   "id": "flyback",
   "title": "Typical connection: flyback secondary",
   "page": 2,
   "description": "A single-switch flyback whose output diode is replaced by Q1, an N-MOSFET in the return leg of the secondary, driven by U1. VD reads Q1's drain at the winding end and VS reads its source, so the chip sees VDS directly; VGATE drives Q1 through Rg. U1 draws its supply from the output rail through Rdc, smoothed by Cdc. OVT and EN are both tied to VCC, which keeps the part enabled and selects the largest turn-off offset. RMOT to ground sets the minimum on time. On the primary, Rs and Cs form a snubber across the winding and Ci decouples the input.",
